# The hero's left-facing walk body. F09 was added 2026-09-23; the rest
# predate this file's header.
#
# F09 was missing because its constant was doing two jobs. CV_0020 named
# BOTH the shared-bank offset 0x0020 (a 49x20 ten-leaf figure) and, in
# LAKE, the CINEMATIC bank's offset 0x0020 (a 1x0 single dot drawn five
# times per iteration of DRAW_4_DROPLETS_LOOP). `video type=0` selects the
# shared bank and plain `video` selects the per-stage cinematic one, so one
# name covered two unrelated pictures, and dos/LAKE carried TWO
# `CV_0020 EQU 0x0020` definitions, one in each sense.
#
# The droplet sense is now CINEMATIC_DROPLET_SPRINKLE_DOT, which freed the
# name. Four independent lines put this piece at F09:
#
#   declaration  dos/LAKE.asm declared its second CV_0020 EQU directly
#                between HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F08 and _F10 -- the family's
#                own ordering puts it in the F09 slot, and the unified
#                chunk does the same at hero_fall_right_and_drawers.inc
#   offset       0x0020 sits below 0x00B4 (F10), in the second of the two
#                offset regions this family occupies
#   geometry     49.0x20.0 with 10 leaves, the ONLY live CV with a body
#                shape anywhere below 0x00B4
#   phase width  F10..F14 widths (23.5, 26.5, 26.0, 22.0, 18.0) repeat
#                F02..F06 exactly, so F09 must repeat F01's 20.0 -- and
#                this piece is 20.0 wide
#
CV_037C HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F00
CV_0764 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F01
CV_0790 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F02
CV_07BC HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F03
CV_07E8 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F04
CV_0814 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F05
CV_0844 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F06
CV_0874 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F07
CV_08A0 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F08
CV_0020 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F09
CV_00B4 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F10
CV_0128 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F11
CV_01B0 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F12
CV_0234 HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F13
CV_02AC HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY_F14
CV_09F6 HERO_STAND_NEUTRAL_BODY
